ithub.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1828192075","pull_request_review_id":2413815864,"id":1828192075,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5s9_9L","diff_hunk":"@@ -1684,13 +1684,19 @@ void SceneTreeDialog::_show_all_nodes_changed(bool p_button_pressed) {\n }\n \n void SceneTreeDialog::set_valid_types(const Vector<StringName> &p_valid) {\n-\tif (p_valid.is_empty()) {\n-\t\treturn;\n+\tif (allowed_types_hbox) {\n+\t\tallowed_types_hbox->queue_free();","path":"editor/gui/scene_tree_editor.cpp","commit_id":"d5176757c0bfca35f6040b825f6a3201edbdf136","original_commit_id":"df673ee77d49d5d8b0ca0a6595c69df3cd842748","user":{"login":"jasonmorgado","id":21321412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzIxNDEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21321412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado","html_url":"https://github.com/jasonmorgado","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonmorgado/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I've added the changes from the recent batch of comments.\r\n\r\nThis one appears to be the solution to the mysterious errors I couldn't figure out earlier. 🎉 \r\n\r\nThis fix immediately fixed the random message I mentioned:\r\n`core/object/object.h:1036 - Condition \"slot >= slot_max\" is true. Returning: nullptr`\r\n\r\nAlso notably, the code used to be\r\n```\r\ncontent->remove_child(allowed_types_hbox);\r\nallowed_types_hbox->queue_free();\r\n```\r\nAnd the remove_child actually did crash occasionally. (when quickly toggling between options) I figured remove_child was redundant with the queue_free after so I took it out. \r\n\r\nremove_child seems to work fine with the nullptr added. I hear mixed things about whether a remove_child() is needed before a queue_free. It seems redundant but I see it everywhere in the codebase. Do you think it's worth adding it back?","created_at":"2024-11-04T18:23:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T18:23:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98558#discussion_r1828192075","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98558","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1828192075"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98558#discussion_r1828192075"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98558"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1828192075/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1688,"original_line":1688,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1827079820,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"position":7,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1828199449","pull_request_review_id":2413827616,"id":1828199449,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5s-BwZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -5297,6 +5297,32 @@ void AnimationTrackEditor::_add_track(int p_type) {\n \t\treturn;\n \t}\n \tadding_track_type = p_type;\n+\tVector<StringName> valid_types;\n+\tswitch (adding_track_type) {\n+\t\tcase Animation::TYPE_METHOD:\n+\t\tcase Animation::TYPE_BEZIER:\n+\t\tcase Animation::TYPE_VALUE: { // \"Property\" track\n+\t\t} break;","path":"editor/animation_track_editor.cpp",